{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/381488-share-your-villians-part-2-electric-boogalo","id":381488,"title":"Share your Villians part 2 Electric boogalo","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-25T18:47:12-08:00","id":381488,"title":"Share your Villians part 2 Electric boogalo","content":"So, i decided to post some of the bad guys im planing to use, in case it inspires someone else.<br /> <br /> The Willinkers: At first they seem normal, perhaps too normal.<br /> its a family clan of 10 members, mostly elderly. the youngest member is Philip Wilinker (60 years old), they are a troupe of &quot;Tourists&quot; who travel on winnebagos and such. always carrying cameras, always seeming soo friendly and &quot;Christians.&quot;.<br /> They are NOT supernatural beings, they are a normal family. They dont have anything supernatural or weird about them, they go around passing as old tourists with RVs. Whats creepy about them is how Unasuming they are and how Normal or even Invisible they come. the world of darkness is a mirror of our ours, under that notion, they pass unsuspected as a group of tourists who take pictures about everything and talk about their grankids or relatives. Maybe even approaching the PC asking him or her for some help, maybe one of them cant open his pill container, or they are lost on the highway. they will look very kind and even a bit senile, weak even. if the PC helps them, they might offer him for a ride or for some dinner.<br /> they will eat normally, talking about normal subjects and suddenly, before you can tell. one of them will try and stab you or poison you.<br /> <br /> They are murderers, cannibals and even rapists...and Why are this way? is it a Bane? is it Vengeance? are they ghouls or nephandi?..No, they do this and act this way because &quot;They Can get away with it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T06:31:52-08:00","id":381868,"title":"","content":"The Seelie Court has been the dominant one ever since the Resurgence and the return of the sidhe. While not safe and friendly the way modern fairy tales might make them out to be, the Seelie are the Court more devoted to preserving and cultivating the creatifity of Man, and thus the more hopeful one for the Fae. But there are whispers and rumors of a time not too long ago by Faerie standards when the Unseelie Court was in ascendancy. A time when most of the sidhe had fled, and were gone from this world, and things seemed even colder and banal than they do now. And those rumors speak of a master of one of the Unseelie Courts: the Lord of Winter.<br /> <br /> The traditional Samhain festivities create a rolicking night for the one-day show of an Unseelie Court. In some Freeholds, where the commoners have told their returned Lords of this legend, it is become traditional to appoint a Lord of Winter - a Changeling masterful in pranks and the more feverish sort of revelry - to bring some dark mirth to the night of Unseelie rule. This chosen Changeling is knighted by the &quot;passing&quot; lord of the Seelie Court, who turns rulership over along with the sword Vinternacht - not the real one, if such ever existed, of course, just a prop, a fanciful piece of terrifying glamour or chimerical steel.<br /> <br /> There are, however, those - both Seelie and Un- - who view this new tradition with trepidation. For the Lord of Winter was said to have earned the loyalty of his Unseelie followers by virtue of one important thing: when the Shattering occurred, he did not abandon them. The Lord of Winter, say they, is a true sidhe lord, cold and terrible and with plans, prior to the Resurgence, to save the Changelings by risking their destruction. They find little amusing in the gifting of a false Vinternacht; the real blade is supposedly the masterwork of a suicidal Nocker whom the Lord of Winter himself Rhapsodized, with the sword as his final creation. Whether out of fear or respect, such Changelings quietly shiver at the mockery of giving this title to whatever Fae will be the ceremonial king of the Samhain festival.<br /> <br /> Winter, cold banality's season, is coming. The Unseelie all agree. Most view it with fatalism, seeking to enjoy the warmth of Autumn while it lasts, even if burning it up hastens its end. But the Lord of Winter, say some, was worse. He sought not to enjoy the warmth, but to hasten Winter for its own sake. For he, mad though he may have been, was its self-proclaimed Lord.<br /> <br /> Mercifully, it is likely he is just a legend, say the returned sidhe. Who would have stayed behind when they could retreat to Arcadia? Who would <i>want</i> to embrace banality and bring about his own destruction? Besides, there's been no sign of such a sidhe in all of the unseelie courts. Surely, by now, he'd have objected?<br /> <br /> <br /> A young sidhe, whose first reincarnation in decades enjoyed a Chrysalis brought about by reuniting with his ancient Seelie lover from before the Shattering, would have little reason to awaken Unseelie. In fact, his own darker urges might frighten him. But a quest by the trolls and redcaps of the court brought back a <i>perfect</i> prop for Vinternacht: a chimerical blade that just looks the part so well, if given a little polish. The pooka who is to be the Unseelie King for this Samhain has been practicing his oath of office. &quot;I will bring the darkness. I am the master of the storm!&quot; He plans some great pranks to pull on the court, and for the court to pull on others!<br /> <br /> The sword terrifies the young sidhe. He refuses to look at it, if he can avoid it. He wants to skip the ceremony, but the nobles of the court absolutely cannot. The mangled oath is just too much to bear. His honor, his pride, will not suffer the mockery and foolishness of these returned cowards. As the cheers rise from the crowd, the sidhe boy's summer-blond hair turns the color of ice, and his cheesy Unseelie costume ripples, somehow more regal. Taking the sword from the pooka too surprised by the interruption to stop this noble who is shifting to his Unseelie aspect, he sheathes the blade in the pooka's chest.<br /> <br /> As the faerie blood and glamour spills from the now-mortal human that is collapsing at his feet, Vinternacht drinks deeply and regains its cold and terrible spleandor. &quot;<i>I</i> am the darkness. <i>I</i> am the storm. I <i>am</i> the Lord of Winter!&quot;<br /> <br /> And now that he has reclaimed his title, he will bring down winter upon all the Earth and its Changeling prisoners. Harsh. Bitter. Merciless banality. For the harsher the winter, the shorter it must be.<br /> <br /> After all, without Winter, how can there ever be a Spring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:42:22-08:00","id":386212,"title":"","content":"The Shadow<br /> <br /> Children are dying. They are found by parents and siblings, still tucked into their beds, no marks on them, no signs of poison or sickness. Several dozen have died in the past two months, and the police are baffled. They might have been smothered, but the families come up clean, and home security shows no signs of break-in. It isn't environmental, and it isn't medical. They die without regards to their socio-economic status, their general health, their race.<br /> <br /> Only a handful of people know the full extent of the deaths, and they are starting to notice potential patterns. The children were all under 9 years of age, they slept alone or with an infant sibling. And with each new death, another pin is added to the map of the city, and they can see that whatever is doing this, is striking neighborhood after neighborhood as it heads in towards the city's densest population center. The rate of deaths seems to be increasing in anticipation of that day.<br /> <br /> They will try to stop it, these police and doctors and scientists, but they won't look in the right places. They expect to find a person, a murderer who leaves a trace. What they won't be looking for is a living shadow, a being who feeds on the terror of a child's last breath, and then tucks its victim back into bed. And really, in a world full of shadows, how do you stop one that wants to kill?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":966,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","user":"Redford_Blade","date":". 01-30-2015, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:58:06-08:00","id":386256,"title":"","content":"i recently writte up a Mummy Warlord of egypt and africa, very The Mandarin meets Gadaffi sort of guy. he is insane, rutheless and he only wants power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}